3B.1 — What the Brain Actually Is

CNS Brain is the mechanism responsible for maintaining and advancing a cognitive process.

It performs:

OBSERVE
→ UNDERSTAND
→ FRAME
→ RETRIEVE
→ HYPOTHESIZE
→ INVESTIGATE
→ PREDICT
→ CHALLENGE
→ DELIBERATE
→ DECIDE
→ ACT
→ OBSERVE OUTCOME
→ LEARN
→ REASSESS

But this does not mean every task must pass through every stage.

A trivial task may be:

OBSERVE → ANSWER → STOP

A major investment decision may require the full loop.

Core principle

> Cognitive depth must match problem complexity, uncertainty and consequence.




