3B.11 — Information Value

The Brain should consider whether additional investigation is worth doing.

Conceptually:

\[
VOI(q)
=
E[\max_a U(a|E,q)]
-
\max_a E[U(a|E)]
-
Cost(q)
\]

But this is not frozen as a mandatory mathematical implementation.

Initial CNS may approximate it using:

decision consequence
× uncertainty
× probability information changes decision
÷ investigation cost

Later, measured data can justify a more formal model.

This prevents us from building sophisticated mathematics before CNS has evidence that it needs it.


